      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "1. A: Huáng Kēzhǎng, Huáng Tàitai,   Section Chief Huáng, Mrs. Huáng--\n      huānyíng, huānyíng.             welcome.\n   A: Qǐng jìn.                       Please come in.\n\n2. B: Fù Tàitai, nín hǎo?             How are you, Mrs. Franklin?\n   B: Zhè shi yìdiǎn xiǎo yìsi.       Here is a small token of appreciation.\n\nNote on Nos. 1-2\n\nXiǎo yìsi: You have already seen yìsi in the expression yǒu yìsi, \"to be interesting.\" Yìsi means \"meaning,\" \"significance,\" \"intention,\" \"idea.\" In No. 2, above, xiǎo yìsi (literally, \"small (good) intent\") is an idiomatic expression meaning \"a small (token of my) feelings of appreciation.\"\n"
